<title>FINLAND: NOKIA WINS $35 MLN GSM NETWORK DEAL.</title>
<headline>NOKIA WINS $35 MLN GSM NETWORK DEAL.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish telecommunications group Nokia said in a statement on Friday it had won a $35 million GSM network expansion order from Bellsouth in New Zealand.</p>
<p>&quot;The new contract is estimated to be worth around $NZ50 million ($35 milion) and is part of Bellsouth's accelerated coverage expansion programme,&quot; Nokia said.  </p>
<p>Nokia said it will supply high capacity mobile switching centres and the latest generation of Nokia base station sub systems in the three main centres, together with istallation, comissioning and support service.</p>
<p>Nokia has been in co-operation with Bellsouth over the past five years, it said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 245</p>
</text>
